lass="readMoreWrapper" style="height: auto; -webkit-line-clamp: 3;"><span><abbr>The Kinder Institute of Life Planning and The Moules are two pioneering organizations dedicated to transforming professional and organizational life by putting people first. At the heart of both lies a commitment to trust, empathy, and fiduciary principles\'97not as regulatory obligations, but as vibrant ways of being that elevate performance, profitability, and meaning.\
The Kinder Institute trains financial professionals to put their clients\'92 lives first. Through its EVOKE\'ae trainings, advisors learn to uncover each client\'92s most profound goals and values, integrating them with sound financial strategies. Founded by George Kinder, the Institute has long championed the view that financial planning is life planning\'97a deeply human process that empowers clients to live purposeful, free, and fulfilled lives.\
Now, with the launch of The Moules\'97a global startup founded under the UK\'92s Innovator/Founder visa\'97Kinder is expanding this philosophy beyond financial services. The Moules brings Fiduciary In All Things (FIAT) into enterprises as an emerging, organic culture, rather than a checklist of policies. Through the Three Domains Workshops (3DW), The Moules offers immersive trainings that infuse workplaces with energy, productivity, empathy, deep listening, and trust\'97aligning the aspirations of individuals with the enterprise\'92s mission.\
While many organizations struggle with disengaged teams, uninspired values statements, and lackluster cultures, The Moules works from the inside out. It cultivates environments where personal and professional purposes are welcomed and strategically integrated\'97transforming people\'92s aspirations into business assets and culture into a driver of sustained energy and success.\
Together, the Kinder Institute and The Moules model a future in which fiduciary values are the foundation for thriving relationships\'97between advisor and client, leader and employee, enterprise and society. \
Kinder's main purpose in attending Future Proof is in a vendor capacity.</abbr></span></span></div></div></div><div class="selectable_card_dataRow"><div class="selectable_card_dataWrapper"><label class="selectable_card_dataWrapper_label">Country</label><div class="selectable_card_dataWrapper_displayVal"><ul><li>United Kingdom</li></ul></div></div><div class="selectable_card_dataWrapper"><label class="selectable_card_dataWrapper_label">US State</label><div class="selectable_card_dataWrapper_displayVal">-</div></div></div><div class="selectable_card_dataRow"><div class="selectable_card_dataWrapper"><label class="selectable_card_dataWrapper_label">Company Type</label><div class="selectable_card_dataWrapper_displayVal"><ul><li>Professional Services Firm</li></ul></div></div><div class="selectable_card_dataWrapper"><label class="selectable_card_dataWrapper_label">Investor Type: Company</label><div class="selectable_card_dataWrapper_displayVal">-</div></div><div class="selectable_card_dataWrapper"><label class="selectable_card_dataWrapper_label">Company Size: Employees</label><div class="selectable_card_dataWrapper_displayVal"><abbr>10 or fewer</abbr></div></div></div><div class="selectable_card_dataRow"><div class="selectable_card_dataWrapper isFullWidth"><label class="selectable_card_dataWrapper_label">Solutions &amp; Services: Offering</label><div class="selectable_card_dataWrapper_displayVal"><ul><li>Estate Planning</li><li>Family Office Services</li><li>Financial Planning</li><li>Infrastructure</li><li>Marketing and Communications Services</li><li>Philanthropy and Charitable Giving Services</li><li>Practice Management Solutions</li><li class="moreButton"><span class="tooltipIconWrapper"><span>+ 3 More</span></span></li></ul></div></div></div><div class="selectable_card_dataRow"><div class="selectable_card_dataWrapper isFullWidth"><label class="selectable_card_dataWrapper_label">Solutions &amp; Services: Interested in</label><div class="selectable_card_dataWrapper_dis